166
00:06:17,077 --> 00:06:18,238
Its customers,

167
00:06:18,238 --> 00:06:21,293
worried about long-term access to memory,

168
00:06:21,293 --> 00:06:23,425
were lining up for contracts lasting

169
00:06:23,425 --> 00:06:24,973
several years.

170
00:06:25,217 --> 00:06:27,471
By September twenty twenty-six,

171
00:06:27,471 --> 00:06:28,837
TrendForce said suppliers had

172
00:06:28,837 --> 00:06:31,569
significantly curtailed memory for

173
00:06:31,569 --> 00:06:33,307
consumer products.

174
00:06:33,307 --> 00:06:35,923
That is why consumer memory was expected

175
00:06:35,923 --> 00:06:37,936
to see the strongest price increases of

176
00:06:37,936 --> 00:06:38,737
all.

177
00:06:39,137 --> 00:06:40,294
The phone in your pocket and the

178
00:06:40,294 --> 00:06:41,741
laptop on your desk were now competing

179
00:06:41,741 --> 00:06:43,478
for silicon with the biggest data centers

180
00:06:43,478 --> 00:06:44,037
on Earth.

181
00:06:44,037 --> 00:06:46,607
And it was not only Micron.

182
00:06:46,797 --> 00:06:48,194
According to Nikkei,

183
00:06:48,194 --> 00:06:50,624
the leading manufacturers could meet only

184
00:06:50,624 --> 00:06:53,034
about sixty percent of global demand,

185
00:06:53,034 --> 00:06:55,254
even with their expansion plans.

186
00:06:55,517 --> 00:06:58,917
High prices usually attract a challenger.

187
00:06:58,987 --> 00:06:59,920
This time,

188
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:02,771
one was waiting in China.

189
00:07:08,417 --> 00:07:11,384
Can a newcomer break into a market

190
00:07:11,384 --> 00:07:13,333
this hard to enter?

191
00:07:17,417 --> 00:07:17,947
CXMT,

192
00:07:17,947 --> 00:07:20,989
China's largest memory chipmaker,

193
00:07:20,989 --> 00:07:21,837
